module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- verifyProof — the kernel's three proof-term rules, Fenel-bodied.
-- expr-substrate Phase 6b0 (brief:
-- `workstreams/expr-substrate/briefs/phase-6b0-prover-fenel-port.md`).
--
-- THE TRUST BOUNDARY, PORTED. `engine/src/kernel.ts`'s `verify` (Phase 4,
-- pre-ts-elimination TS) re-checks a proof term against a proposition. The
-- RULE LOGIC — dispatch on the proof-term tag, the Refl equality ladder,
-- the DecidableSetResult kind↔proposition agreement + witness re-check
-- routing + re-decide consumption, the SampleTestResult shape checks —
-- lives HERE now. The TS `verify` is a thin delegate that (a) extracts the
-- two `$tag`s, (b) pre-computes Fenel value equality for Refl and structural
-- representation equality for anti-repurpose witnesses at the host boundary,
-- (c) pre-computes
-- the set-algebra re-decide for the proposition's shape (`isSubset` /
-- `isDisjoint` / `decideEmpty` — the re-run CALL is the justified bridge;
-- the TS set-algebra dispatchers themselves already route through the
-- Fenel `set-algebra-deciders.fenel` mirrors where ported), and (d) maps
-- the outcome marker back to the `VerifyResult` `$tag` shapes.
--
-- OUTCOME MARKERS (plain records, the P5/6a `$`-key barrier — a `.fenel`
-- body cannot author `{$tag: …}` shapes, and EpistemicStatus stays TS-side
-- output grading per the 6b Q1 lock):
--   { tag = "Ok",  status = "Proven" | "SolverChecked" }
--   { tag = "Ok",  status = "SampleTested", samples = n }
--   { tag = "Err", etag = "WitnessRejected" | "UnknownRule", reason }
--   { tag = "Err", etag = "ShapeMismatch", reason, propositionTag, proofTag }
--   { tag = "Err", etag = "NonTotal", reason }   (unified-static-analysis 3g)
--
-- PRE-COMPUTED FACTS (the `eqs` record + `decision` string + `verdict` string):
--   eqs.lhsRhs       — structuralEq(prop.lhs, prop.rhs)        (Refl)
--   eqs.lhsValue     — structuralEq(prop.lhs, proof.value)     (Refl)
--   eqs.witnessLeft  — deepEqual(prop.s, proof.witness.left)    (DecidableSet)
--   eqs.witnessRight — deepEqual(prop.t, proof.witness.right)   (DecidableSet)
--   decision         — "true" | "false" | "unknown" — the re-decide outcome
--                      for the proposition's own (s, t) per its $tag (read
--                      ONLY after the shape + witness checks pass, exactly
--                      like the TS original's post-check re-run)
--   verdict          — "Total" | "Unknown" | "Partial" | "" — the SUBJECT
--                      function's totality verdict TAG (unified-static-analysis
--                      Phase 3g — THE SOUNDNESS PAYLOAD). Computed by the shipped
--                      Fenel `analyze`/`totalityVerdict` (TS marshal seam:
--                      `subjectTotalityVerdict`); the SampleTestResult/PropForall
--                      arm REJECTS when it is "Unknown" or "Partial" (a ∀ proven
--                      by sampling a non-total function is unsound — the samples
--                      may diverge or the "all passed" is vacuous). "" = no
--                      subject function declared (the proof names no Fenel
--                      function whose totality is in question — the gate is
--                      inert, exactly as for Refl over arbitrary host values).
--                      The OTHER proof rules (Refl / DecidableSetResult) do NOT
--                      consult it — neither quantifies over a function's
--                      totality (D-3g-2: the gate is SampleTestResult-only).
--
-- The TS-quirk PRESERVED: when `proof.kind` is none of subset/disjoint/
-- empty, the original falls past the three kind-guards straight into the
-- proposition-$tag switch (a bogus kind with a matching witness still
-- re-checks). `vpDecidable`'s final else mirrors that, byte-faithfully.
--
-- NO ENTITY DECLS HERE: outcome markers stay plain records. The ONE new
-- entity — the `Judgment` currency (JEmpty / JInhabited) — lives in the sibling
-- `judgment.fenel`, alongside the decomposition iso
-- (`judgmentOfProposition` / `evidenceOfProofTerm`), the single `verifyJudgment`
-- core, and the kernel-primary `verifyWitnessMembership` singleton face.
--
-- decide-substrate Phase 2 (K1) — THE CUT. The 4-case decidable-set switch
-- (`vpDecideTwo`/`vpDecideOne`/`vpDecideInhabited`) is RETIRED, subsumed by the
-- one lattice judgment: `verifyProof` is now the presentation dispatcher over
-- (Judgment, Evidence); `vpDecidableSwitch` builds the judgment + delegates the
-- re-check to `verifyJudgment`. Refl + SampleTestResult stay presentation rules
-- (constraints §1.1 shallow-enum-eq / §1.4 unmaterialised ⟦P⟧). Wire UNCHANGED
-- (Proposition/ProofTerm still cross every boundary) ⇒ byte-identical markers.
--
-- decide-substrate Phase 2 (K3) — the kernel ACCEPTS JUDGMENT CLAIMS. The
-- ReDecide evidence arm dispatches on the claim's nature (`vpReDecide`): a
-- JEmpty/JInhabited claim (the judgment-native currency the producers emit
-- since K2) routes to `vpJudgment` — the shared shape recognizer
-- (`recheckPlan`, judgment.fenel) recovers the plan {kind, s, t}, the
-- kind↔shape agreement guards mirror vpDecidable's, and the claim goes
-- STRAIGHT to `verifyJudgment` (it IS the judgment — no iso rebuild). The
-- K1-landed witness-membership rule is WIRED here: `DecidableSetResult{kind:
-- "witness", witness: {left: w}}` proves a JInhabited claim by the {w} ⊆ s
-- re-check (verifyWitnessMembership). Closed-sum Prop* claims keep the
-- vpDecidable presentation path (compat — retires at K4). Refl/Sample evidence
-- over a judgment claim flows through the existing propTag guards (natural
-- ShapeMismatch). The eqs facts for judgment claims are computed by the TS
-- delegate from the SAME plan (witness anti-repurpose against the recognized
-- original (s, t)).
-- =========================================================================

@label "Verify proof"
@description "The kernel's trust-boundary re-checker, Fenel-bodied (expr-substrate Phase 6b0; re-derived onto the one lattice judgment decide-substrate Phase 2). The PRESENTATION DISPATCHER: classifies the proof term via evidenceOfProofTerm (Refl / ReDecide / Sample / Unknown), then Refl proves PropEq via the pre-computed structural-equality facts (the singleton-equality presentation); ReDecide (DecidableSetResult) decomposes the proposition to a JEmpty/JInhabited judgment (judgmentOfProposition) and re-checks it through the single verifyJudgment core (kind↔proposition agreement + witness re-check + the pre-computed tri-precision decision); Sample (SampleTestResult) proves PropForall via the totality gate + propertyId/allPassed/samplesChecked shape checks. Returns a plain-record outcome marker ({ tag = Ok, status } / { tag = Err, etag, reason }); the TS delegate maps it to VerifyResult and grades EpistemicStatus (TS-side output grading, the 6b Q1 lock). Unknown proof-term tags ⇒ the UnknownRule TCB guard."
@tags "engine" "kernel" "prover" "expr-substrate" "phase-6b0"
verifyProof : (propTag: String) -> (proofTag: String) -> (prop: a) -> (proof: a) -> (eqs: a) -> (decision: String) -> (verdict: String) -> a
verifyProof propTag proofTag prop proof eqs decision verdict =
  let ev = evidenceOfProofTerm proofTag
  if eq ev "Refl" then vpRefl propTag eqs
  else if eq ev "ReDecide" then vpReDecide propTag proofTag prop proof eqs decision
  else if eq ev "Sample" then vpSample propTag proofTag prop proof verdict
  else { tag = "Err", etag = "UnknownRule", reason = concat "kernel: no rule for proof term '" (concat proofTag "' (Phase 4 supports Refl / DecidableSetResult / SampleTestResult only)") }

-- vpReDecide — the ReDecide evidence dispatcher (decide-substrate Phase 2 K3):
-- a JUDGMENT claim (JEmpty / JInhabited — the K3-native currency the producers
-- emit) routes to the judgment-claim rule (vpJudgment); a closed-sum Prop*
-- claim routes to the compat presentation path (vpDecidable — dies at K4).
@label "kernel: vpReDecide"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 2 K3 — the ReDecide evidence dispatcher: JEmpty/JInhabited claims (the judgment-native currency) route to vpJudgment (shape-recognized re-check + the witness-membership arm); closed-sum Prop* claims route to vpDecidable (the compat presentation path, retiring at K4). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "kernel" "prover" "judgment" "decide-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
vpReDecide : (propTag: String) -> (proofTag: String) -> (prop: a) -> (proof: a) -> (eqs: a) -> (decision: String) -> a
vpReDecide propTag proofTag prop proof eqs decision =
  if eq propTag "JEmpty"
  then vpJudgment propTag proofTag prop proof eqs decision
  else if eq propTag "JInhabited"
  then vpJudgment propTag proofTag prop proof eqs decision
  else vpDecidable propTag proofTag prop proof eqs decision

-- vpJudgment — the JUDGMENT-claim ReDecide rule (decide-substrate Phase 2 K3).
-- The claim IS the judgment (no iso rebuild); the plan (shape + original (s,t))
-- comes from the shared recognizer (recheckPlan, judgment.fenel). Arms:
--   kind "witness"  ⇒ THE witness-membership rule (K1-landed, WIRED here):
--                     requires a JInhabited claim; re-checks {w} ⊆ s via
--                     verifyWitnessMembership (proof.witness.left carries the
--                     ELEMENT w; the claim's set is plan.s). SolverChecked.
--   kind "mu-induction" ⇒ THE Park (Knaster-Tarski) rule (decide-substrate
--                     Phase 8μ.2 — the first new trusted-kernel rule since the
--                     witness rule): requires a subset-shaped JEmpty claim
--                     (plan.kind "subset"); re-checks μv.F ⊆ T via
--                     verifyMuInduction — which RE-DERIVES the premise F[v:=T]
--                     from the claim's recognized (s = μv.F, t = T), so a bogus
--                     proposer witness is never consulted. SolverChecked.
--   kind subset/disjoint/empty/nonempty ⇒ kind↔shape agreement (the vpDecidable
--                     guard discipline over the RECOGNIZED shape), then the
--                     polarity-gated re-check (vpJudgmentGo → verifyJudgment).
--   unrecognized kind ⇒ falls straight to the re-check (the preserved TS quirk:
--                     a bogus kind with a matching witness still re-checks).
@label "kernel: vpJudgment"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 2 K3 — the judgment-claim ReDecide rule: fetch the shared recheck plan (shape + original (s,t)); kind witness ⇒ the witness-membership rule (JInhabited only — re-checks {w} ⊆ s via verifyWitnessMembership, the K1-landed singleton face now WIRED); kinds subset/disjoint/empty/nonempty ⇒ kind↔recognized-shape agreement then the polarity-gated verifyJudgment re-check; unrecognized kinds fall through to the re-check (the preserved quirk). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "kernel" "prover" "judgment" "witness" "decide-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
vpJudgment : (propTag: String) -> (proofTag: String) -> (prop: a) -> (proof: a) -> (eqs: a) -> (decision: String) -> a
vpJudgment propTag proofTag prop proof eqs decision =
  let plan = recheckPlan propTag prop
  if eq proof.kind "witness"
  then
    if eq propTag "JInhabited"
    then verifyWitnessMembership proof.witness.left plan.s
    else vpMismatch propTag proofTag "DecidableSetResult{kind:witness} proves an inhabited (JInhabited) claim, not an emptiness claim"
  else if eq proof.kind "mu-induction"
  then
    if eq plan.kind "subset"
    then verifyMuInduction plan.s plan.t
    else vpMismatch propTag proofTag "DecidableSetResult{kind:mu-induction} requires a subset-shaped JEmpty claim (μX.F ⊆ T)"
  else if eq proof.kind "subset"
  then
    if eq plan.kind "subset"
    then vpJudgmentGo prop plan eqs decision
    else vpMismatch propTag proofTag "DecidableSetResult{kind:subset} requires a subset-shaped JEmpty claim (s ∩ ¬t)"
  else if eq proof.kind "disjoint"
  then
    if eq plan.kind "disjoint"
    then vpJudgmentGo prop plan eqs decision
    else vpMismatch propTag proofTag "DecidableSetResult{kind:disjoint} requires a disjoint-shaped JEmpty claim (s ∩ t)"
  else if eq proof.kind "empty"
  then
    if eq plan.kind "empty"
    then vpJudgmentGo prop plan eqs decision
    else vpMismatch propTag proofTag "DecidableSetResult{kind:empty} requires a bare JEmpty claim"
  else if eq proof.kind "nonempty"
  then
    if eq plan.kind "nonempty"
    then vpJudgmentGo prop plan eqs decision
    else vpMismatch propTag proofTag "DecidableSetResult{kind:nonempty} requires a JInhabited claim"
  else vpJudgmentGo prop plan eqs decision

-- vpJudgmentGo — the polarity-gated re-check for a judgment claim: the claim
-- IS the judgment, so it goes straight to verifyJudgment with the arity flag +
-- messages keyed on the RECOGNIZED kind (the same strings vpDecidableSwitch
-- uses — one message vocabulary across both presentation paths).
@label "kernel: vpJudgmentGo"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 2 K3 — the judgment claim's polarity-gated re-check: verifyJudgment over the claim itself (it IS the judgment) with twoSided + witness/recheck messages keyed on the recognized plan kind (subset/disjoint two-sided; empty/nonempty one-sided; the same message strings as the Prop* presentation path). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "kernel" "prover" "judgment" "decide-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
vpJudgmentGo : (prop: a) -> (plan: a) -> (eqs: a) -> (decision: String) -> a
vpJudgmentGo prop plan eqs decision =
  if eq plan.kind "subset"
  then verifyJudgment prop eqs decision true "DecidableSetResult{kind:subset} witness must match the proposition's (s, t)" "isSubset re-check did not return `Just true` for the witnessed pair"
  else if eq plan.kind "disjoint"
  then verifyJudgment prop eqs decision true "DecidableSetResult{kind:disjoint} witness must match the proposition's (s, t)" "isDisjoint re-check did not return `Just true` for the witnessed pair"
  else if eq plan.kind "empty"
  then verifyJudgment prop eqs decision false "DecidableSetResult{kind:empty} witness must match the proposition's s" "decideEmpty re-check did not return `Just true` for the witnessed set"
  else verifyJudgment prop eqs decision false "DecidableSetResult{kind:nonempty} witness must match the proposition's s" "decideEmpty re-check did not return `Just false` (set is empty / undecided) for the witnessed set"

-- vpRefl — Rule 1: Refl x proves PropEq T x x (structural equality).
@label "kernel: vpRefl"
@description "Phase 6b0 — the Refl rule: requires a PropEq proposition, lhs ≡ rhs, and the proof's carried value ≡ lhs (the pre-computed Fenel value-equality facts). Ok ⇒ Proven. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "kernel" "prover" "expr-substrate" "phase-6b0"
@category "engine-internal"
vpRefl : (propTag: String) -> (eqs: a) -> a
vpRefl propTag eqs =
  if not (eq propTag "PropEq")
  then { tag = "Err", etag = "ShapeMismatch", reason = concat "Refl is a proof of PropEq, not " propTag, propositionTag = propTag, proofTag = "Refl" }
  else if not eqs.lhsRhs
  then { tag = "Err", etag = "WitnessRejected", reason = "Refl requires lhs ≡ rhs (structural equality), but the operands differ" }
  else if not eqs.lhsValue
  then { tag = "Err", etag = "WitnessRejected", reason = "Refl carries a `value` that must equal both PropEq operands" }
  else { tag = "Ok", status = "Proven" }

-- vpDecidable — Rule 2: the three kind-guards, then the proposition switch.
@label "kernel: vpDecidable"
@description "Phase 6b0 — the DecidableSetResult rule's kind↔proposition agreement guards: kind subset/disjoint/empty/nonempty each requires the matching Prop* tag (nonempty ⇒ PropInhabited, expr-substrate Phase 6b); a non-matching pair ⇒ ShapeMismatch. Past the guards (including the preserved TS quirk: an unrecognised kind falls straight through), routes to the proposition-tag switch. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "kernel" "prover" "expr-substrate" "phase-6b0"
@category "engine-internal"
vpDecidable : (propTag: String) -> (proofTag: String) -> (prop: a) -> (proof: a) -> (eqs: a) -> (decision: String) -> a
vpDecidable propTag proofTag prop proof eqs decision =
  if eq proof.kind "subset"
  then
    if eq propTag "PropSubset"
    then vpDecidableSwitch propTag proofTag prop eqs decision
    else vpMismatch propTag proofTag "DecidableSetResult{kind:subset} requires a PropSubset proposition"
  else if eq proof.kind "disjoint"
  then
    if eq propTag "PropDisjoint"
    then vpDecidableSwitch propTag proofTag prop eqs decision
    else vpMismatch propTag proofTag "DecidableSetResult{kind:disjoint} requires a PropDisjoint proposition"
  else if eq proof.kind "empty"
  then
    if eq propTag "PropEmpty"
    then vpDecidableSwitch propTag proofTag prop eqs decision
    else vpMismatch propTag proofTag "DecidableSetResult{kind:empty} requires a PropEmpty proposition"
  else if eq proof.kind "nonempty"
  then
    if eq propTag "PropInhabited"
    then vpDecidableSwitch propTag proofTag prop eqs decision
    else vpMismatch propTag proofTag "DecidableSetResult{kind:nonempty} requires a PropInhabited proposition"
  else vpDecidableSwitch propTag proofTag prop eqs decision

-- vpDecidableSwitch — the proposition-$tag switch, re-derived onto the one
-- lattice judgment (decide-substrate Phase 2). Each decidable-set shape builds
-- its judgment via `judgmentOfProposition` (subset ⇒ JEmpty (s ∩ ¬t); disjoint
-- ⇒ JEmpty (s ∩ t); empty ⇒ JEmpty s; inhabited ⇒ JInhabited s) and hands it to
-- the single `verifyJudgment` core with the arity flag (subset/disjoint =
-- two-sided witness) + the per-shape witness/recheck messages. The retired
-- `vpDecideTwo`/`vpDecideOne`/`vpDecideInhabited` cluster is subsumed: one core,
-- byte-identical markers. Any other proposition tag ⇒ the 'not a proof of'
-- ShapeMismatch.
@label "kernel: vpDecidableSwitch"
@description "decide-substrate Phase 2 — the DecidableSetResult rule's proposition switch, re-derived onto the one lattice judgment: each decidable-set shape decomposes via judgmentOfProposition (subset/disjoint/empty ⇒ JEmpty, inhabited ⇒ JInhabited) and routes to the single verifyJudgment core (two-sided witness for subset/disjoint; polarity-gated tri-precision decision — JEmpty accepts \"true\", JInhabited accepts \"false\"); any other proposition tag ⇒ the 'not a proof of' ShapeMismatch. Subsumes the retired vpDecideTwo/vpDecideOne/vpDecideInhabited cluster. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "kernel" "prover" "judgment" "decide-substrate" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
vpDecidableSwitch : (propTag: String) -> (proofTag: String) -> (prop: a) -> (eqs: a) -> (decision: String) -> a
vpDecidableSwitch propTag proofTag prop eqs decision =
  if eq propTag "PropSubset" then verifyJudgment (judgmentOfProposition propTag prop) eqs decision true "DecidableSetResult{kind:subset} witness must match the proposition's (s, t)" "isSubset re-check did not return `Just true` for the witnessed pair"
  else if eq propTag "PropDisjoint" then verifyJudgment (judgmentOfProposition propTag prop) eqs decision true "DecidableSetResult{kind:disjoint} witness must match the proposition's (s, t)" "isDisjoint re-check did not return `Just true` for the witnessed pair"
  else if eq propTag "PropEmpty" then verifyJudgment (judgmentOfProposition propTag prop) eqs decision false "DecidableSetResult{kind:empty} witness must match the proposition's s" "decideEmpty re-check did not return `Just true` for the witnessed set"
  else if eq propTag "PropInhabited" then verifyJudgment (judgmentOfProposition propTag prop) eqs decision false "DecidableSetResult{kind:nonempty} witness must match the proposition's s" "decideEmpty re-check did not return `Just false` (set is empty / undecided) for the witnessed set"
  else vpMismatch propTag proofTag (concat "DecidableSetResult is not a proof of " propTag)

-- vpSample — Rule 3: SampleTestResult proves PropForall.
-- unified-static-analysis Phase 3g — THE KERNEL GATE. The `verdict` pre-computed
-- fact is the SUBJECT function's totality verdict tag. A `PropForall x. P(x)`
-- proven by SAMPLE-TESTING `P` is UNSOUND when `P` (or a function it tests) is
-- non-total: the samples may diverge (never counted), or the "all passed" rests
-- on a function with no well-defined values. So a verdict of "Unknown" or
-- "Partial" REJECTS the proof BEFORE any shape check — a non-total subject is
-- never certified, regardless of the claim's shape validity. "Total" (proven
-- terminating) and "" (no Fenel-function subject declared ⇒ gate inert, the
-- synthetic/abstract-property case) proceed to the existing shape checks. This
-- is the ONLY rule that consults `verdict` (D-3g-2: SampleTestResult-only).
@label "kernel: vpSample"
@description "Phase 6b0 + 3g — the SampleTestResult rule: requires a PropForall proposition, matching propertyId, allPassed = true, and at least one sample checked. Phase 3g gates it on the SUBJECT function's totality verdict (the pre-computed `verdict` fact): \"Unknown\"/\"Partial\" ⇒ Err NonTotal (a ∀ sample-tested over a non-total function is unsound), checked BEFORE the shape checks; \"Total\"/\"\" proceed. Ok ⇒ SampleTested with the sample count (the kernel verifies the claim's SHAPE — it doesn't re-iterate; empirical evidence stays graded SampleTested, not Proven). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "kernel" "prover" "expr-substrate" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3g"
@category "engine-internal"
vpSample : (propTag: String) -> (proofTag: String) -> (prop: a) -> (proof: a) -> (verdict: String) -> a
vpSample propTag proofTag prop proof verdict =
  if eq verdict "Unknown"
  then { tag = "Err", etag = "NonTotal", reason = "SampleTestResult cannot prove a universal over a subject function whose totality is Unknown — the checker has not proven it terminates, so the sampled `∀` may be vacuous (diverging samples are never counted)" }
  else if eq verdict "Partial"
  then { tag = "Err", etag = "NonTotal", reason = "SampleTestResult cannot prove a universal over a subject function that is Partial (declared @partial / provably non-total) — the universal rests on a function with no well-defined values everywhere" }
  else if not (eq propTag "PropForall")
  then { tag = "Err", etag = "ShapeMismatch", reason = concat "SampleTestResult is a proof of PropForall, not " propTag, propositionTag = propTag, proofTag = proofTag }
  else if not (eq prop.propertyId proof.propertyId)
  then { tag = "Err", etag = "WitnessRejected", reason = concat "SampleTestResult propertyId '" (concat proof.propertyId (concat "' does not match the proposition's '" (concat prop.propertyId "'"))) }
  else if not proof.allPassed
  then { tag = "Err", etag = "WitnessRejected", reason = "SampleTestResult reports allPassed = false (a counterexample exists)" }
  else if lte proof.samplesChecked 0
  then { tag = "Err", etag = "WitnessRejected", reason = "SampleTestResult requires at least one sample checked" }
  else { tag = "Ok", status = "SampleTested", samples = proof.samplesChecked }

-- vpMismatch — the four-field ShapeMismatch marker builder.
@label "kernel: vpMismatch"
@description "Phase 6b0 — build the ShapeMismatch outcome marker carrying reason + propositionTag + proofTag (the structured fields callers branch on). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "kernel" "prover" "expr-substrate" "phase-6b0"
@category "engine-internal"
vpMismatch : (propTag: String) -> (proofTag: String) -> (reason: String) -> a
vpMismatch propTag proofTag reason =
  { tag = "Err", etag = "ShapeMismatch", reason = reason, propositionTag = propTag, proofTag = proofTag }
